	(text "Same relays and terminal as the MES2_Extension \"WINCH CONTROL\": TE IM03GR, 5 V coil (178 Ω, 28 mA) from\n+5V_24, contacts 2 A / 220 VDC, 60 W DC. They only switch the 48 V winch controller's direction inputs to\nJ18 pin 2 (COM): pin 1 = CLK, pin 3 = ACLK. They are not rated for the winch motor current.\nTE terminal assignment: coil 1 (+) / 8 (-); pole 1: 3 COM, 2 NC, 4 NO; pole 2: 6 COM, 7 NC, 5 NO.\n\nDrivers as on the relay sheets (CIF §7a): AO3400A, 100 Ω gate, 100k pull-down, so both relays are OFF\nduring reset and boot (PA0 / PA1 float then). The Extension used 2SC2884 transistors without a pull-down.\n\nHardware interlock (new, uses the spare second pole): CLK closes COM → ILK_CLK → K5 NO1 → CLK only\nwhile K6 rests (its NC2 feeds ILK_CLK), and the same the other way. If both relays are energised, both\noutputs stay open, so the winch can never see both directions at once. Firmware still drives only one."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 156.21 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
		(uuid "9465dbe7-00e0-5747-b637-fa915c993023")
	)
	(rectangle
		(start 201.93 20.32)
		(end 403.86 147.32)
		(stroke (width 0) (type dash))
		(fill (type none))
		(uuid "bd9ea4ea-e8a2-5115-b390-038009c61215")
	)
